{"name":"Solar Power","hex":"#f4b435","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"solar power","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The conversion of energy from sunlight into electricity, either directly using photovoltaics, indirectly using concentrated solar power, or a combination of the two."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/solar_power"}],"entries":[{"title":"Solar Power (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Solar Power is the third studio album by New Zealand singer-songwriter Lorde. It was released on 20 August 2021 by Universal. Inspired by the death of her Golden Retriever mix dog and her visit to Antarctica in 2019, the album was written with producer Jack Antonoff to capture themes of solipsism and summer escapism. It mainly focuses on Lorde's leisure time in her homeland, New Zealand, while simultaneously expressing her disdain for fame and celebrity culture."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/Lorde_-_Solar_Power.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_Power_(album)","wikidata":"Q107184476"},{"title":"Solar Power (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Solar Power\" is a song by New Zealand singer-songwriter Lorde, released on 11 June 2021 as the lead single from her third studio album of the same name. The song was written and produced by Lorde and Jack Antonoff and released to radio stations by Universal. Inspired by the 1990 single \"Loaded\" by Scottish band Primal Scream and early 2000s music, \"Solar Power\" is an indie folk, psychedelia, and sunshine pop song, marking a departure from Lorde's electronic and melancholia music styles. The lyrics of the song depict summer escapism set on a beach."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_Power_(song)","wikidata":"Q107177492"},{"title":"Solar power","blocks":[{"text":"Solar power, also known as solar electricity, is the conversion of energy from sunlight into electricity, either directly using photovoltaics (PV) or indirectly using concentrated solar power. Solar panels use the photovoltaic effect to convert light into an electric current. Concentrated solar power systems use lenses or mirrors and solar tracking systems to focus a large area of sunlight to a hot spot, often to drive a steam turbine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Electrical_and_Mechanical_Services_Department_Headquarters_Photovoltaics.jpg/330px-Electrical_and_Mechanical_Services_Department_Headquarters_Photovoltaics.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solar_power","wikidata":"Q1483757"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Cicadoidea.jpg/500px-Cicadoidea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Cicadoidea.jpg/500px-Cicadoidea.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lorde recorded cicadas on her phone to incorporate nature in the album's production.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACicadoidea.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3f/Lorde_Solar_Power_censored_cover.jpg/250px-Lorde_Solar_Power_censored_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/3/3f/Lorde_Solar_Power_censored_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/3/3f/Lorde_Solar_Power_censored_cover.jpg/250px-Lorde_Solar_Power_censored_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Digitally altered cover artwork","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALorde_Solar_Power_censored_cover.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum